{
  "_comment": [
    "Festival and public-holiday dataset for ncal.",
    "",
    "'fixed'    - same BS month/day every year. A BS month begins on its sankranti by",
    "             construction, so every sankranti is simply day 1 of its month and",
    "             needs no astronomy of its own.",
    "'ad_fixed' - same Gregorian month/day every year.",
    "'lunar'    - a hand-verified date pinned to one BS year, which OVERRIDES the",
    "             computed rule of the same name in rules.json. Tithi-based festivals",
    "             are computed, not tabulated; this exists only for the occasional",
    "             observance the government moves for reasons no ephemeris predicts.",
    "",
    "'lunar_years_covered' is the inclusive [first, last] BS year range those overrides",
    "cover. BS 2082: the gazette put Jitiya on Bhadra 30, a day after its udaya ashtami."
  ],

  "lunar_years_covered": [2082, 2082],

